CLUB: BIG SKY CONTESTERS
CREATED-BY: N1MM Logger+ 1.0.10888.0
SOAPBOX: Almost spectacular condx on all bands except 160 with lots of activity. SFI and
SOAPBOX: SN well over 200. My first attempt in this 5 year old evolving contest. I had
SOAPBOX: planned to operate only a few hours looking for interesting DX but got sucked
SOAPBOX: into the addictive radio contest vortex.
SOAPBOX: Too many purists and competitive contesters consider FT a garbage mode and
SOAPBOX: ignore it. It's like watching the grass grow or the paint dry they say. FT8 is
SOAPBOX: painfully slow but FT4 keeps the rate reasonable. I do FT some, mainly because
SOAPBOX: of its very impressive technology and presence of more rare DX.
SOAPBOX: For most seasoned operators, the mode is supposed to be a low power weak signal
SOAPBOX: experience, so I ran 100 watts for the first 9 hours on the high bands. Not a
SOAPBOX: peep seen or heard on 10 but 15 and 20 were wall to wall. After dinner, it was
SOAPBOX: hard to maintain a run tone freq with low power and so much QRM, plus too many
SOAPBOX: callers on my freq and busted exchanges. So I decided to add 6dB. That helped
SOAPBOX: make it more interesting working almost everything I saw, but I broke the low
SOAPBOX: power golden rule for FT. 15 stayed open to midnight local and 20 well past
SOAPBOX: then. So we missed the earlier 40 EU opening.
SOAPBOX: The FT4 sub-bands were well behaved but got cleaned out rather quickly so we had
SOAPBOX: to watch more paint dry on FT8. About half the stations Q'd there did not know a
SOAPBOX: contest was on and sent only a signal report. The call history file helped there
SOAPBOX: some but we did have to ask for grid squares too often. The WW Digi website has
SOAPBOX: an excellent Tip Sheet on how best to run in this event and deal with that
SOAPBOX: issue: https://ww-digi.com/operating.htm. For any digi contest, update WSJT-X
SOAPBOX: to the current version V2.7.0 so logging and exchange formatting are correct.
SOAPBOX: Along with the current version of N1MM+ logging, it worked pretty well for me
SOAPBOX: except for not highlighting dupes.
SOAPBOX: As this contest evolves and continues to work out various rules changes and
SOAPBOX: software/logging issues, it's going to keep growing and become hugely popular.
SOAPBOX: It seems most new hams coming into the hobby prefer either PTT or FT8. I predict
SOAPBOX: it will rival the CQ and ARRL majors in just a few years. JMHO
